stromligning_entities.description:
Cable Juice Planner ({prefix}) uses Strømligning sensors that are disabled or that Strømligning does not provide. A missing sell tariff counts as 0, which makes the calculated sell price too high, and without the price sensors the stored prices are used.

Disabled in Home Assistant (Strømligning disables its excl. VAT sensors by default – enable them under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities**, with *Show disabled entities*):
{disabled}

Not provided by Strømligning (e.g. the price forecasts are off in its options):
{not_provided}

This repair disappears by itself when the sensors work again.

solcast_entities.description:
Cable Juice Planner ({prefix}) can't use all the Solcast forecast sensors it needs, so the days without one are planned from the weather forecast and the stored solar history instead. Solcast disables the forecast sensors of day 3 and on by default.

Disabled in Home Assistant (enable them under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities**, with *Show disabled entities*):
{disabled}

Not named the way Cable Juice Planner expects (the entity id must end in _today, _tomorrow or _day_3 …):
{renamed}

Without hourly detail (turn on *Hourly detail* under *Forecast attributes breakdown* in the Solcast options):
{no_detail}

This repair disappears by itself when the sensors are fixed.

entities_missing.description:
Cable Juice Planner ({prefix}) reads these entities, but they are disabled in Home Assistant, or they are neither in the entity registry nor in the states (renamed or deleted). The plan can't use them.

Disabled (enable them under **Settings → Devices & services → Entities**, with *Show disabled entities*):
{disabled}

Missing (check the entity id in the Cable Juice Planner settings, or the integration that provides it):
{missing}

After the fix, run the charger test: turn on **Test my charger automation** under *Settings* on the dashboard. This repair disappears by itself when the entities are enabled or found again.
